&lt;h1&gt;Senior Backend Engineer - Platform&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Piramidal is looking for a backend engineer to help build and scale the infrastructure behind our real time neural monitoring platform. You&#39;ll work on hard problems: high throughput streaming, real-time analytics, and hospital grade reliability. You’re a chronic optimist and relentlessly resourceful.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a full-time role based in our New York office (5 days a week), with required travel to client sites. Candidates must have US work authorization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;In this role you will&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and run Python and Go services that consume, transform, and serve real-time streams of neurological data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, maintain, and improve data models, ingestion pipelines and retention for high frequency time series data, from raw neurological data, to all time series derived from it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and extend the APIs behind clinical workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with ML engineers to take models from research to production inference, and keep them running there.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make the platform observable and dependable: metrics, alerting, capacity planning, and incident follow-up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help build software to the standards of a regulated medical device, including cybersecurity, traceability and change control.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Your background looks something like&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of building and operating backend systems in production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can own a problem from an ambiguous start to a running, monitored service, and you can explain your decisions verbally and in writing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Real experience with event-driven or stream-processing systems: partitioning, checkpointing, backpressure, and at-least-once delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong Python, including concurrency (threads vs. processes, asyncio) and testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with containerization and orchestration, preferably using kubernetes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid relational database skills, from schema design to query performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Nice to have&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Go, especially for networked or low-latency services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Azure: Event Hubs, Service Bus, Web PubSub, Blob Storage, AKS.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apache Arrow, Parquet or other columnar formats.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Video streaming, storage, and processing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Systems where sub-second latency matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data engineering or warehousing at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Model serving (PyTorch)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work in healthcare or other regulated software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About Us&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’ve built the first-of-its-kind foundation model for brainwave data. Our goal is Intelligence Amplification (IA) by means of creating neural decoders that enable interactions with the language of neurons. Powered by our SOTA foundation model, our first product detects in real time abnormalities in the brains of ICU patients.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Compensation &amp;amp; Benefits&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Base salary range: $200,000 – $300,000, depending on experience and skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meaningful equity plan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive health coverage, including premium medical, dental, and vision plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Daily lunch budget.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monthly gym subscription.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Interview Process&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Initial Screen&lt;/strong&gt; (30 min): Discussion to ensure timelines, experience, and expectations align.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Screen &lt;/strong&gt;(1 hour): via Google Meet&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Final Round (in person)&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coding Problem (1 hour)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;System Design (1 hour)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Product Session (1 hour)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Questions (20 minutes)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;h1&gt;Senior Product Manager&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Piramidal is looking for a product manager to own the roadmap and execution of our real-time neural monitoring platform. You&#39;ll be responsible for translating what clinicians need into what engineers build.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;In this role you will&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the product roadmap across our clinical and infrastructure products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run discovery with clinicians and partners to translate needs into product requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and prioritize features across detection, alerting, visualization, workflow, and more&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work directly with ML and platform engineers on technical tradeoffs and model behavior&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with regulatory and quality teams to ensure product decisions align with submission and safety constraints&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ship product in short cycles with a small, fast-moving team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Your background looks something like&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of product management in a technically complex and/or fast-moving domain&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working directly with engineering teams on system design and technical tradeoffs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with clinical or regulated products (FDA or equivalent)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written communication&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to move fast and independently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Nice to have&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clinical domain knowledge in neurology or critical care&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with real-time or streaming data products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in ML-powered products where model behavior is a core product surface&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with FDA clearance processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About Us&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are building a first-of-its-kind foundation model for electrophysiological brain data. Our goal is to create scaled neural decoders that enable humans to understand and control neural syntax. Our flagship product brings a state-of-the-art seizure detection model into real-time clinical workflows, helping clinicians detect and respond to seizures faster.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a software engineer to help us build Piramidal’s flagship product. You&#39;ll be responsible for building and maintaining the system that enables performant web experiences for our users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In this role you will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and implement Piramidal’s flagship user interface.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with product, design, and ML engineering teams to deliver cohesive web experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement real time visualizations for high dimensional data streams using websockets and performance oriented charting libraries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Optimize performance for critical web components.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Your background looks something like:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of practical experience as a frontend engineer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise in modern JavaScript frameworks, particularly React and NextJS (ie, “backend-of-the-frontend” subject matter expertise).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience optimizing web application performance and measuring metrics like ARS.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Strong candidates may have:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in building infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with frontend monitoring and alerting systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with TypeScript and strong typing systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with frontend performance optimization techniques on real-time data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A portfolio&amp;nbsp; of high-quality, scalable web applications in production environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are building a first-of-its-kind foundation model for electrophysiological brain data. Our goal is to create scaled neural decoders that enable humans to understand and control neural syntax. Our flagship product brings a state of the art seizure detection model into real time clinical workflows, helping clinicians detect and respond to seizures faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Interview Process&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Initial Screen&lt;/strong&gt;: 30 minute discussion to ensure timelines, experience and expectations align.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Screen&lt;/strong&gt;: 1hr&amp;nbsp; live via Google Meet.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Final Round&lt;/strong&gt;: Technical design question (1hr),Product sense (30 min), Q&amp;amp;A (15min).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
